{"kind":"request","text":"Stop the review gate refusing work whose only fault is that the world moved. An artifact naming an exact immutable commit does not stop naming that commit because a basis upstream was superseded, and judging whether the movement matters is exactly what a reviewer is for. This blocked four separate pieces of work on 2026-08-09 and is independent of how the describes-versus-reasoned-from proposal is decided.","body":{"conditions":"Separate the two facts the projection fuses. Artifact.Stale is currently retired[event] || stale[event], and liveArtifact in spike/cmd/gs/main.go refuses on it with the message 'artifact is stale or retired', which names the conflation. Expose retired and stale as distinct fields; the fold already computes DescribesSupersededWorld, SuccessionUnrecorded and LivePredecessors separately, so the finer signal exists and is being discarded at the gate. gs review must refuse an artifact that is retired or ineffective, and must accept one that is merely stale, recording the staleness and its cause in the verdict body so the report states that the world had moved and the reviewer signed anyway. gs merge keeps its current strictness unless the review conditions say otherwise; say which you chose and why. Add a test proving a stale-but-live artifact can be reviewed and a retired one cannot, and check that each fails when the guard is reverted. Do not change what staleness means or how it propagates - that is the ratification's business, not this request's.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}